ts high fire  rate and low recoil  i personally prefer the galil but i  think it's because my memories with the  famas were post patch  that's right this thing got nerfed with  the 1.1 update that shook up the recoil  slowed down the aim down sights time and  widen the bullet spread of its hip fire  this gun is still fun today but it's a  shell of what it once was  long ago  what can i say about the acr we've  talked about it before in our best guns  of call of duty video  where our very own dave jewett kindly  reflects on it as we all do  when you think of the acr you think of  one thing that  recoil or should i say the lack of it  when playing modern warfare 2 back in  2009 this was the first gun i remember  ever being called a laser  it was that legendary steadiness that  popularized it  and even though it wasn't the most  powerful it was a breeze connecting  shots and taking down enemies from just  about any range you can conceive  any attachment you added was simply a  bonus but some fan favorites include the  silencer  and the extended magazine what you're  seeing here is actually footage from  modern warfare 3 where the acr  still kicked ass let's talk about some  of the weapons in call of duty's most  recent title  cold war at the time of recording call  of duty black ops cold war has been out  for less than a month  players were quick to find that the m16  and the og were just  nasty let's put it this way both of them  were nerfed after the game's launch week  they each had their damage ranges  dropped burst delays increased  and reduced effectiveness of the laser  attachment  and you know what they're still good i  played around with the og here and did  so well that my next lobby was filled  with some pretty tough customers  i got work and got a notification saying  to erase the game from my hard drive and  just try again next year  and while i'm here i might as well  mention call of duty 4's m16  this thing was one of the grandfathers  of broken weapons 